  "limitations": "Simple 2D graphics (coloured tiles and rectangles), no textures, no on-foot mode, no weapons, no multiplayer. NPC steering ignores walls except for push-out, so police can get stuck on corners. Real-time behaviour depends on the browser; audio starts only after the first key or touch (browser rule). Input max 64 KB, so maps above about 96x96 tiles do not fit.",
  "port_notes": "Original builder and game runtime by Skillpack contributors. Embedded third-party code: MainLoop.js build/mainloop.min.js (MIT, leading comment with an author URL replaced by the full MIT notice in an HTML comment so the file has no URLs) and ZzFXMicro.min.js (MIT, wrapped in a function so the AudioContext is created only after a user gesture). The configuration JSON is embedded with <, > and & escaped. The runtime implements the formulas of G003 (car), G004 (circle vs box), G006 (seek/arrive/flee/pursuit), G007 (wanted), G008 (missions), G009 (integer money) and G010 (save envelope); tests/test_flow_e2e.py compares them with the Python tools.",
  "flow_role": "Step 12 (HTML üret): the last skill call; the runner writes result.html to index.html, then verifies it (no external URLs, JavaScript syntax, a headless run of the game loop)."
}
